\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Aquatic Elf Racial Penalties
\par }{\fs24 \tab Aquatic elves can be out of water only for a number of days equal to their Fitness scores. They cannot gain the elven attack bonus for bows, as such weapons are ineffective underwater.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Dark Elves
\par }{\b\fs24 Character point cost: 45
\par }{\fs24 The dark elves, also known as drow, live underground. Nearly all of them are evil, and they have used their cunning to become masters of much of the Underdark. Most intelligent creatures shun them. In m
any ways, dark elves are the twisted, corrupt versions of their above\_ground relatives.
\par \tab Drow have jet black skin, the better to hide their movements underground. And they tend to be shorter than other elves. The only other physical difference drow exhibit is their eyes, which glow a feral red\emdash 
evidence, perhaps, of the hatred that burns in their hearts and minds.
\par \tab Very few dark elves are of good alignment, and these are usually player characters.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Languages:}{\fs24  Dark elves begin play with: drow, elf, gray dwarf, illithid, undercommon, kuo\_toa, bugbear, and orcish.
\par 
