\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Gray Elf Racial Penalties
\par }{\fs24 \tab Due to their reclusive and often haughty ways, gray elf characters suffer a \endash 1 reaction roll penalty when dealing with other elves, and a \endash 2 penalty when encountering other races.
\par 
\par }{\fs28 High Elves
\par }{\b\fs24 Character point cost: 40
\par }{\fs24 The most common type of elf, these are 
also the most open, friendly, and cooperative. High elves set the physical standards for elves, being about 5' tall and weighing about 110 pounds. High elves are the palest of all elves, with a skin tone resembling the color of fine cream. High elves usua
l
ly have blond hair and blue eyes or darker hair, ranging from sandy brown to jet black, with intensely green eyes. High elves like to wear pastel shades. When out on a hunt or adventuring in the forest, high elves typically cover themselves in a cloak of 
forest green in the spring and summer and one of tan or russet in the autumn.
\par \tab Most high elves are chaotic good, though as player characters they can be any alignment.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Languages:}{\fs24  High elves begin with high elf, common, elf, gnome, halfling, goblin, hobgoblin, orc, and gnoll.
\par 
