\par }{\fs24 \tab Because high elves are so friendly and open, they often take things\emdash including illusions\emdash at face value. High elves attempting to disbelieve something which is actually an illusion suffer a \endash 2 penalty to the attempt.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Sylvan (Wood) Elves
\par }{\b\fs24 Character point cost: 40
\par }{\fs24 
Sylvan elves, or wood elves as they also are known, descended from the same stock as other elves. However, they prefer to live a more primitive lifestyle, more in touch with their roots in the primeval forests they have made their homes. They are geared t
o
ward simple survival, and they concentrate on their environment rather than on philosophical debates and the study of magic. Sylvan elves enjoy the beauty of a singing bird, the patterns of an intricate spider web, and their own practice of tattooing. The
y are the most temperamental and emotional elves.
\par \tab Sylvan elves are more muscular than other elves, and their complexions are darker. They have yellow to coppery\_red hair and brown eyes, though some rare cases of hazel or blue eyes are known. Any sylvan elf
 born with hazel or blue eyes is considered a good omen for the tribe, believed to be destined for personal greatness. Sylvan elves normally dress in browns and greens, the better to blend in with the forest.
\par \tab Unlike most of their brethren, sylvan elves tend toward neutral alignments, though player characters can be of any alignment.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Languages:}{\fs24  Sylvan elves begin with their own dialect, in addition to elf, centaur, pixie, dry
ad, treant, and brownie. Sylvan elves rarely learn the common tongue, as they wish to have as little to do with the outside world as possible.
\par 
