\par }{\fs28\cf6 Forest Gnomes
\par }{\b\fs24 Character point cost: 45
\par }{\fs24 Forest gnomes are less common than rock gnomes. They fill an important niche in the ecology of the woodlands, caring for small plants and animals that other races some
times overlook. Unlike other gnomes, forest gnomes prefer to make their homes above ground in small log cabins or in large, hollow trees.
\par \tab The smallest of gnomes, they average only 21_2' in height. They share the physique of rock gnomes\emdash though their noses 
are not quite as large. Forest gnomes wear their hair and beards long, and the color runs from brown to black in their youth, fading to gray or white with age. Their skin tends toward a greenish cast to tan, rather like some tree barks, and their eyes are
 blue or brown.
\par \tab Although most forest gnomes are neutral good, player characters can claim any alignment.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Languages:}{\fs24  Forest gnomes speak their own dialect, gnome, treant, dryad, brownie, satyr, and pixie.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Forest Gnomes\rquote  Special Abilities
\par }{\fs24 Animal friendship\tab Melee combat bonuses*
\par Forest movement\tab Saving throw bonus
\par Hide
\par 
\par * Forest gnomes may apply their defensive adjustment when fighting any man\_sized or larger creatures; their racial enemies are orcs, lizard men, troglodytes, or any creature which they have directly observed damaging woodlands.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Forest Gnome Racial Penalties
\par }{\fs24 \tab Forest gnomes cannot have infravision.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Rock Gnomes
\par }{\b\fs24 Character point cost: 40
\par }{\fs24 Rock gnomes are the most common gnomes, and they can be encountered in a variety of climates and environments. 
The most noticeable feature of the rock gnome is his nose. All gnomes have large noses, but rock gnomes sport the biggest noses of all. Rock gnomes love gems, especially diamonds bigger than their noses.
\par \tab Rock gnomes stand about 31_2' tall and weigh about 70 pounds. Eye color is predominately blue, although green or brown are seen occasionally. Their hair is usually white or pale gray.
\par \tab Rock gnomes are typically neutral good, but player characters can choose any alignment.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Languages:}{\fs24  Rock gnome player characters start with: common, dwarf, gnome, halfling, goblin, kobold, and the simple languages of burrowing mammals\emdash moles, badgers, etc.
