\par }{\fs28\cf12 Halfling  }{\fs24 Most halflings are about 3' tall and weigh 60 to 70 
pounds. They are generally plump, with round, broad, and often florid faces. They have curly hair atop their heads and on the tops of their typically bare feet. The average life expectancy of a halfling is 150 years.
\par \tab Halflings are a sturdy and industrious people, generally quiet and peaceful. They enjoy all the creature comforts, and while not overly ambitious, they are friendly and open. Their homes are well\_
furnished burrows, and most of their work is done out in the sunshine. Halflings get along with the others races, including humans, and they can be found in practically any civilization. 
\par \tab The standard halfling subraces are: hairfoot, stout, and tallfellow. Halfling characters can be of the following classes: cleric, fighter, or thief. The race\rquote s multi\_class options are limited to fighter/thief.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Players who choose halflings for their characters have 35 character points to spend on racial abilities.}{\fs24  These points can be spent to customize a halfling from the general skill list below, or they can be used to purchase a subrace
\rquote s skill package. Only 5 points can be retained for use later in the character creation process.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Hairfoot Halflings
\par }{\b\fs24 Character point cost: 30
\par }{\fs24 The most common halfling, hairfoots prefer rural settings. They are a practical people, and t
here are many bakers, millers, farmers, and innkeepers in their society. Averaging 3' tall, hairfoots are stockier than their cousins. Their complexions run from pale peach to ruddy to dark brown, and their eyes are usually black or dark brown. Their hair
 can be blond, brown, red, black, and shades in between\emdash though with few exceptions it is always curly. Hairfoots are distinguished from other halflings by their lack of facial hair.
\par \tab Most hairfoots are lawful good, though player characters can be of any alignment.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Languages:}{\fs24  Hairfoots can begin with any four halfling, human, or elf dialects.
\par 
