\par }{\fs28\cf6 Stout Halflings
\par }{\b\fs24 Character point cost: 35
\par }{\fs24 
Stouts are not as common as hairfoots, and they tend to be stockier. As a result, they also tend to be stronger. Stouts usually live apart from human societies, choosing instead to live near dwarves. There may be some dwarven blood somewhere in the stouts
\rquote  ancient past.
\par \tab Ruddy in complexion, stouts vividly blush when pleased or embarrassed. Their hair tends to be light, and their eyes usually are blue, gray, or green. They favor practical, sturdy clothes, such as well\_cured leather. They are the most indust
rious of all halflings, and are even comfortable around bodies of water and boats.
\par \tab Most stouts are lawful good, though players can choose any alignment for their characters.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Languages:}{\fs24  Stouts can begin with any six halfling, human, or dwarven dialects.
