\par \tab The paladin is a noble and heroic warrior\emdash often literally the knight in shining armor\emdash a symbol of all that is right, good, and just in the world. Examples of paladins include Sir Lancelot, Sir Gawain, Sir Galahad of King Arthur\rquote 
s Round Table, and Roland and the 12 Peers of Charlemagne. For more on these men, see }{\i\fs24 Charlemagne\lquote s Paladins}{\fs24  Historical Reference book for the AD&D game. Such a warrior has high ideals to maintain at all times.
\par \tab Only humans can become paladins. A paladin must be lawful good in alignment. Any paladin who changes alignment los
es all his special powers. This loss might be temporary or permanent, depending on the circumstances. A paladin who consciously commits a chaotic act must find a lawful good cleric of at least 7th level, confess the act, and seek penance. If a paladin kno
wingly commits an evil act, the character\rquote 
s status as a paladin is forever lost. If such an act is committed by the paladin under duress (enchanted or controlled by magic), the loss of status remains in effect until the paladin completes a major quest for t
he cause of good. The paladin gains no experience points for this quest, but if successfully completed, he regains the status and powers of his paladinhood. All paladins have the following restrictions:
\par 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\fs24 Cannot possess more than 10 magical items. Further, these items must not exceed one set of armor, one shield, four weapons (magical arrows and bolts don\rquote t count), and four other objects.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\fs24 Can never retain wealth. He can keep enough treasure to support himself, pay his henchmen, and so on, but all exces
s monies must be donated to worthy causes. Other characters do not qualify as worthy causes. In addition, 10% of all treasure garnered must be given to a lawful good religious institution of the paladin\rquote s choice.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\fs24 Cannot attract a body of followers. However, he can hire soldiers and specialists\emdash so long as those individuals are lawful good.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\fs24 Will not abide the company of those he knows to be evil. Those of other alignments will be tolerated as long as they behave themselves.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\fs24\highlight3 
Paladins receive 60 character points with which to purchase class abilities. Each of the abilities below cost 5 to 10 character points. Any unspent points can be used to acquire nonweapon proficiencies or saved for use during the game. A standard paladin 
spends his character points to acquire the abilities of circle of power 5, curative 10, detection 5, faithful mount 5, healing 5, health 5, protection from evil 5, saving throw bonus 10, and turn undead 10.}{\fs24 
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Circle of power (5):}{\fs24  If the paladin has a }{\i\fs24 holy sword}{\fs24 , he can project a circle of power 10' in diameter. This circle dispels hostile magic at a level equal to the experience level of the paladin
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Curative (10):}{\fs24  Cure diseases of all types once a week for every five experience levels. For example, a 10th level paladin can use his }{\i\fs24 cure disease}{\fs24 
 ability two times a week. (This ability is ineffective against lycanthropy.)
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Detection (5):}{\fs24  Detect evil monsters or creatures up to 60' away by concentrating. A paladin can do this as often as he wishes, but each use takes one round.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Faithful mount (5):}{\fs24  The paladin can summon a special steed at 4th level. This faithful steed might not be a horse\emdash 
it may be any creature the DM deems appropriate. This steed is bonded to the paladin. However, this steed does not simply appear when called. The paladin likely must find his mount in a memorable way, such as on a quest.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Healing (5):}{\fs24  The ability to heal himself or another by the}{\i\fs24  laying on of hands}{\fs24  once a day. The paladin can restore two hit points per his experience level.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Health (5):}{\fs24  Immunity to all forms of disease. (Paladins are not immune to lycanthropy and mummy rot.)
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Poison resistance (10):}{\fs24  The character gains a +1 bonus to all saving throws versus poison.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Priest spells (10):}{\fs24  The }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote s Handbook}{\fs24  states that at 9th le
vel a paladin can cast priest spells from the following spheres: combat, divination, healing, and protection. However, by purchasing this ability, paladins can cast spells beginning at 4th level. Paladins do not gain extra spells for possessing high Intui
tion scores, nor can they cast spells from cleric or druid scrolls. The spell progression chart for paladins appears below.
\par 
