\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Protection from evil (5):}{\fs24  The paladin has a natural aura with a 10' radius. Within this aura, summoned or evil creatures suffer a \endash 
1 penalty to all attack rolls. Creatures affected by this aura know the paladin to be the source of their discomfort.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Resist charm (10):}{\fs24  Paladins with this ability gain a +2 bonus to saving throws versus charm\_like spells and abilities.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Saving Throw Bonus (10):}{\fs24  Paladins with this ability gain a +2 bonus to all saving throws.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Turn undead (10):}{\fs24  When the paladin attains 3rd level he can turn undead. Thi
s ability functions as if the paladin were a cleric two levels lower. For example, a 6th level paladin would turn undead as a 4th level cleric. See the Player\rquote s Handbook for information on turning undead.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Weapon specialization (10): }{\fs24 This paladin can specialize in a particular weapon. The character point cost must be met in addition.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Optional Restrictions
\par }{\fs24 A paladin can gain bonus character points to spend on the above abilities by accepting voluntary restrictions on his warrior abilities. The restrictions are the same as those listed for Fighters.
