\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Bribe* (5):}{\fs24  A thief can bribe an official with gifts of money or merchandise. Only one bribe can be attempted per target. If the attempt fai
ls, the DM should make a reaction roll for the target to determine how he counters the bribe.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Climb walls* (5):}{\fs24  This skill lets thieves climb smooth or vertical surfaces.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Defense bonus (10):}{\fs24  +2 bonus to Armor Class when unarmored and unencumbered.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Detect illusion* (10):}{\fs24  Thieves can see detect illusions within their line of sight, up to 90 feet away. They perceive the illusion as a translucent image, seeing through it as though it were a light mist.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Detect magic* (10):}{\fs24  Thieves can spot magical radiations within their line of sight, up to 60 feet away. They can determine the intensity of the magic\emdash dim, faint, moderate, strong, and overwhelming.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Detect noise* (5):}{\fs24  This is the ability to hear sounds others usually can\rquote t.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Escaping bonds* (10):}{\fs24  There comes a time in every thief\rquote 
s career when his luck runs out and the he is apprehended. The ability to escape bonds such as ropes, leather thongs, manacles, chains, and even straight jackets is a feat of contortion and determination. The thief must roll to break e
very device binding him. If he\rquote s tied at the wrists and at the ankles, then he must make two successful rolls to free himself. This skill takes five rounds to use. A thief might hurry his efforts, but he suffers a \endash 
5% penalty for each round he tries to shave. Locked items also require the thief to successfully pick the locks. A failure on any attempt means that the thief cannot loose that bond or pick the lock.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Find/remove traps* (10):}{\fs24  Many people try to protect their important belongings from thieves with small mechanical traps or alarms. As a result, thieves have developed skills to find and disarm these traps.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Followers (5/10):}{\fs24  By purchasing this skill, a thief can gain followers as described in the }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote s Handbook}{\fs24  if he establishes a stronghold and is at least 10th level. If this is purchased as a 10\_
point ability, the thief can attract followers whenever he establishes a stronghold, regardless of level. Refer to the thief section of the Player\rquote s Handbook for more details on followers.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Hide in shadows* (5):}{\fs24  A thief can attempt to disappear in shadows, bushes, and crannies. A successful thief will be effectively invisible as long as he remains all but motionless. Slow, deliberate movements are allowed.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Move silently* (5):}{\fs24  This is the ability to move without making noise. The movement rate of a thief attempting this is reduced to 1/3 his normal rate. 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Open locks* (10):}{\fs24  A thief can try to pick all types of locks using skill, tools, finesse, and luck. If a thief fails to open a lock, he cannot attempt to open that lock again until advancing a level.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Pick pockets* (10):}{\fs24  A thief uses this skill to pilfer small items from the pouches, pockets, belts, sleeves, packs, etc. of others. A failed attempt means the thief did not come away with an item, but it does
 not indicate the thief was caught in the act. To determine if a thief\rquote s attempt was noticed, subtract three times the victim\rquote s experience level from 100. If the thief\rquote 
s roll was equal to or higher than this number, the attempt was noticed. For example, if the thief tried to pick the pocket of a 5th level fighter and failed\emdash and the thief\rquote s roll was 85 or higher\emdash the thief is noticed. (5x3 = 15. 100
\endash 15 = 85.)
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Read languages* (5):}{\fs24  A thief needs every edge he can get, and the ability to read languages can help.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Scroll use (5/10):}{\fs24  At 10th level, a thief can use magical spell scrolls. By purchasing this skill as a 10\_point ability, he has a chance to read scrolls at any level. If a thief fails to accurately read the scroll, usu
ally something detrimental occurs, such as the spell backfiring. Consult Table 25 for the thief\rquote s chance to read a scroll:
\par 
