\par }{\fs28\cf12 Priests}{\fs24   A priest is a follower and advocate of a particular fantasy deity\emdash most often one of a group, or pantheon, of deities. He acts in a manner appropriate to his deity, and uses his powers and skills to help others 
advance the beliefs of his religion.
\par \tab All priest characters can cast spells granted them by their deity, wear many types of armor, and use many weapons.
\par \tab Priest spells are divided into Spheres of Influence, which mirror the interests of the priest\rquote s deity.
 A priest either has Major or Minor access to a sphere. Major access means that a priest potentially can cast any spell in that sphere. Minor access indicates that the priest can cast only first\_ through third\_
level spells from that sphere. The spell progression for a priest is presented below.
