\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Casting reduction (5):}{\fs24  The cleric\rquote s spell casting time is reduced by 1. All spells still retain a minimum casting time of 1.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Detect evil (10):}{\fs24  Clerics with this ability can see emanations of evil from creatures or objects within a path 10 feet wide by 60 feet long. It takes one round to s
can a direction, and the cleric cannot be attempting other actions.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Detect undead (10):}{\fs24  Clerics can detect all undead within a path 10 feet wide by 60 feet long. It takes one round to scan a direction, and the cleric cannot be attempting other actions. Cl
erics cannot detect undead through stone or other thick materials.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Expert healer (5):}{\fs24  This ability allows the character to cast one }{\i\fs24 cure light wounds}{\fs24  spell a day in addition to the number of spells the priest can normally cast.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Followers (5/10):}{\fs24  By purchasing this skill, a cleric can gain followers as described in the}{\i\fs24  Player\rquote s Handbook}{\fs24  if he establishes a stronghold and is at least 8th level. If this is purchased as a 10\_
point ability, the cleric can attract followers whenever he establishes a stronghold, regardless of level. Refer to the priest section of the Player\rquote s Handbook for more details on followers.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Hit point bonus (10):}{\fs24  Clerics with this ability use 1d10 to determine their hit points rather than 1d8.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Know alignment (10):}{\fs24  This ability allows the character to cast the }{\i\fs24 know alignment}{\fs24  spell once a day. This is in addition to the number of spells the priest can normally cast.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Resist energy drain (5):}{\fs24  Priests with this ability gain a +1 bonus to saving throws vs. the energy drain spell and the level\_
draining attacks of undead. If the attack does not normally allow a saving throw, this ability has no effect. This ability\rquote s saving throw bonus does apply to characters protected by the negative plane protection spell.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Spell duration increase (10):}{\fs24  The duration of all non\_instantaneous spells cast by the cleric increases by 1 round for every two experience levels of the cleric. For example, a 6th level cleric has his spells\rquote 
 durations increased by 3 rounds.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Turn undead (10):}{\fs24  The cleric is granted power ov
er undead, such as zombies, skeletons, vampires, and liches. Clerics can drive away these creatures, and as clerics advance in faith and experience levels, they can destroy some forms of undead. Below is the chart for turning undead.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Warrior\_priests (10):}{\fs24 
 Priests who select this ability use the warrior Strength and Constitution bonuses for exceptional scores. For example, a priest could have an 18/30 Strength, and he could gain bonus hit points for having a Constitution score greater than 16.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Weapon allowance (5):}{\fs24 
 A priest with this ability can choose a favored edged weapon of his deity. For example, a cleric of the elven deity Corellon Larethian could use a long sword, or a priest of the Norse god, Odin might wield a spear. The character must still purcha
se proficiency in the allowed weapon.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Weapon specialization (15): }{\fs24 This priest can specialize in a particular weapon. The character point cost must be met in addition.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Wizardly priests (15):}{\fs24  These priests gain access to one school of wizard spells and can cast them as if they were clerical spells. The priests must continue to observe the number of various level spells they can cast each day.

