\par }{\fs28\cf6 Specialty Priests
\par }{\fs24 \tab Specialty priests are encountered in campaigns where DMs develop or i
mport a mythos or a particular pantheon of deities. The many possible types of specialty priests go beyond the scope of this book. However, players and DMs interested in designing these priests should consult the }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote s Handbook}{\fs24 
, the }{\i\fs24 Complete Priests Handbook}{\fs24 , and the }{\i\fs24 Legends & Lore}{\fs24  book. One example of a specialty priest, the druid, is presented below.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Druids
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx2880\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\b\fs24 Ability Requirements:\tab }{\fs24 Wisdom 12
\par \tab Charisma 15
\par }{\b\fs24 Prime Requisite:}{\fs24 \tab Wisdom, Charisma
\par }{\b\fs24 Allowed Races:}{\fs24 \tab Human, half\_elf
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab 
The druids of history lived among the Germanic tribes of Western Europe and Britain during the days of the Roman Empire. They acted as advisors to tribal chieftains. They believed the earth was the mother of all things, and they revered it, the sun, the m
oon, and certain trees as deities.
\par \tab Druids in the AD&D game are nature priests, protecting pristine woodlands from the depredations of monsters and civilization. They are only loosely based on their historical namesakes.
\par \tab A druid is allowed to wear only leather armor and use only wooden shields\emdash natural materials. A druid may use only the following weapons: club, sickle, dart, spear, dagger, scimitar, sling, and staff.
\par \tab A druid\rquote s standard selection of spells includes major access to the spheres of all, animal, elemental, healing, plant, and weather, and minor access to divination. A druid can use magical items allowed to priests, except for books and scrolls.

\par 
\par \tab }{\fs24\highlight3 A druid has 100 character points to purchase skills. Skills costs 5 to 15 points. Any unspent points can be used to acquire nonweapon proficiencies or saved for use during the game.}{\fs24 
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Access to spheres:}{\fs24  The standard druid selection (see above) costs 60 character points. Or, the druid can purchase spheres individually just as clerics do (see page 57).
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Bonus spell (5):}{\fs24  Once per day the druid can cast an }{\i\fs24 animal friendship}{\fs24  spell. This is a bonus spell and does not count against the druid\rquote s spell total for the day.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Cold resistance (5):}{\fs24  +2 saving throw bonus vs. cold\_ or ice\_based attacks.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Communicate with creatures (10):}{\fs24 
 A druid can acquire the languages of woodland creatures, at the rate of one language per level. For example, a fourth level druid could have four such languages. Some woodland creatures include: centaurs, dryads, elves, fauns, satyrs, gnom
es, dragons, lizard men, manticores, nixies, pixies, sprites, and treants.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Elemental spell bonus (5):}{\fs24  When the druid casts spells from the elemental sphere, all level\_based variables (range, duration, etc.) are calculated as if the druid were one experience level higher than the character\rquote 
s actual level.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Hit point bonus (10):}{\fs24  Druids with this ability use 1d10 to determine their hit points rather than 1d8.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Identify (5):}{\fs24  At 3rd level, a druid can accurately identify plants, animals, and clean water.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Immunity to charm (5/10): }{\fs24 According to the Player\rquote s Handbook, at 7th level a druid becomes immune to charm spells cast by woodland creatures. However, by purchasing this ability for 10 points, a Player\rquote 
s Option druid gains this immunity immediately.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Immunity to disease (10):}{\fs24  A druid with this ability is immune to natural diseases.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Pass without trace (5):}{\fs24  At 3rd level, a druid with this ability can }{\i\fs24 pass without trace}{\fs24 , as per the spell, at his normal movement rate.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Purify water (5):}{\fs24  This ability allows the character to cast one }{\i\fs24 purify food and drink}{\fs24  spell a day in addition to the number of spells he can normally cast.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Fire/Electrical Resistance (5):}{\fs24  a +2 bonus to all saving throws vs. fire and electrical attacks.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Hide in Shadows (5):}{\fs24  A druid can hide in shadows, as the ranger ability, in natural surroundings. See Table 22 in the ranger section for the chance of success.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Move silently (5):}{\fs24  A druid can move silently, as the ranger ability, in natural surroundings. See Table 22 in the ranger section for the chance of success.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Secret language (5):}{\fs24  Druids can speak a secret language only they know, and they use it to converse with each other.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Shapechange (10/15):}{\fs24  According to the Player\rquote s Handbook, at 7th level a druid gains the ability to shapechange. However, by purchasing this skill for 15 character points, a }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote s Option}{\fs24 
 druid gains the following shapechanging abilities:\tab 
\par \tab \tab At 5th level, a druid can change into a bird once a day.\tab 
\par \tab \tab At 6th level, he can also change into a reptile once a day.\tab 
\par \tab \tab By 7th level a druid can also change into a mammal.\tab 
\par \tab The size and shape assumed by the druid can vary from that of a bullfrog or small bird to that of a black bear. The druid can assume the forms of normal creatures only. When assuming a new form, a druid is healed of 10\endash 
60% of any damage he has suffered (round down). The druid also assumes the creature\rquote s physical characteristics (armor class, movement mode and rate, etc.). The druid\rquote s clothing and one item held in each hand also become part of his new shape
\emdash these reappear when the druid resumes his bipedal form.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Weapon specialization (15):}{\fs24  This druid can specialize in a particular weapon. The character point cost must be met in addition.
\par 
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf12 Wizards }{\fs24  Wizards command staggering energies and make dangerous opponents. The power to control magical energies comes from the mind, and as such, Intelligence is very important.
\par \tab Wizards cannot wear armor, as i
t not only interferes with the forces they control, but also goes against their way of thinking. They are limited in the number of weapons that they can wield in combat. Permissible weapons are: knife, dagger, staff, darts, and slings. 
\par \tab All wizards have t
he ability to cast numerous offensive, defensive, and informative spells. The spell progression chart for wizards is below. Just as there are spheres of clerical spells, there also are schools of wizard magic. There are eight schools, and details on them 
can be found in the }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote s Handbook}{\fs24 .
\par \tab Wizards also possess the capacity to use magical items such as wands, rods, staves, rings, scrolls, and potions. Finally, wizards can create new magical spells and items\emdash from scrolls and elixirs to mighty weapons.
\par 
