\par \tab }{\fs24\highlight3 All specialist wizards (illusionists, enchanters, and so on) gain 30 character points to buy skills. The skills below cost 5 to 15 points each. Any remaining points can be spent on nonw
eapon proficiencies or saved for use during the game.}{\fs24 
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Access to schools:}{\fs24  A specialist wizard automatically has access to all schools of magic that are not specifically noted as opposition schools for his specialty. (Note that spells from opposition schoo
ls that happen to be included in alternate schools such as song magic, alchemy, or elemental magic are still not available to the specialist. Wild magic is available only to wild mages.) 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Armored wizard (15):}{\fs24  This wizard can cast spells while wearing the armor of his choice.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Automatic spells (5):}{\fs24  Each time the specialist wizard is able to learn a new level of spells, he can select one spell from his specialty school to learn automatically (without a check).
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Bonus spells (10): }{\fs24 Specialist wizards gain one additional spell per spell level. The extra spell taken must belong to the wizard\rquote 
s school of specialization. For example, a 5th level mage can cast four 1st level spells, two 2nd level spells, and one 3rd level spell. But a 5th level specialist wizard can cast five 1st level spells, three 2nd level spells, and two 3rd level spells
\emdash provided the added spells are from his chosen school.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Casting reduction (5):}{\fs24  The casting time of all the wizard\rquote s spells from his chosen school is reduced by 2. All spells have a minimum casting time of 1.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Combat bonus (10):}{\fs24  A wizard with this ability uses the rogue THAC0 chart.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Detect magic (10):}{\fs24  Characters purchasing this ability can }{\i\fs24 detect magic}{\fs24  once a day for every three levels. For example, a 7th level mage can }{\i\fs24 detect magic}{\fs24 
 twice a day. This is in addition to any }{\i\fs24 detect magic}{\fs24  spells the mage might memorize. The character can spot magical radiations within his line of sight, up to 60' away. He can determine the intensity of the magic\emdash 
dim, faint, moderate, strong, and overwhelming.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Extend duration (10): }{\fs24 The duration of all non\_instantaneous spells from the wizard\rquote 
s chosen school increases by 1 round for every experience level of the caster. For example, if a 6th level necromancer casts a spectral hand spell, it will last 18 rounds rather than 12 rounds.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Intense magic (5):}{\fs24  If a specialist wizard casts a spell from his chosen school, the targets of that spell suffer a \endash 1 saving throw penalty.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Learning bonus (5):}{\fs24  A +15% bonus when attempting to learn new spells belonging the wizard\rquote s school of specialization.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 No components (10): }{\fs24 The ability to designate one specialty\_school spell per character level as a spell that does not require material components. For example, a 3rd\_level specialist may have a total of three spells in his 
spellbook that do not require material components.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Range boost (5):}{\fs24  The reach of all ranged spells (spells with a range other than 0, self, or touch) from the wizard\rquote s chosen school is increased by 25%. For example, the 1st level wizard spell charm person
 has a range of 120 yards. That range is increased to 150 yards.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Read magic (5): }{\fs24 Characters purchasing this ability can }{\i\fs24 read magic}{\fs24  once a day for every two levels. For example, a 4th level mage can}{\i\fs24  read magic}{\fs24  twice a day. This is in addition to any }{
\i\fs24 read magic}{\fs24  spells the mage might memorize.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Research bonus (5):}{\fs24  When attempting to research and create a new spell of his specialized school, treat the spell as one level lower than its actual level.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Saving throw bonus (5):}{\fs24  +1 bonus on saving throws vs. spells cast at them from their school of specialization. This bonus can be purchased several times with a cumulative effect.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Optional Restrictions
\par }{\fs24 \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Learning penalty (5):}{\fs24  A specialist wizard with this restriction suffers a penalty of \endash 15% to all learn spell rolls outside his own specialty.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Limited magical item use (5+):}{\fs24  A wizard with this restriction disdains enchanted items as a crutch for the weak and refuses to use certain categories of magical items. For each category that is barred to him, he gains 5 C
Ps. The categories are: potions, oils, and scrolls; rings, rods, staves, and wands, and miscellaneous magical items; and all weapons and armor.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 More opposition schools (5+): }{\fs24 A specialist wizard with this restriction may choose to take additional opposing 
schools, gaining 5 character points for each additional school in opposition to his specialty. Only standard schools (i.e., those described in the }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote s Handbook}{\fs24 ) can be selected as additional opposition schools.
\par 
\par 
\par }\pard \widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs28\cf12 Psionicist}{\fs24\cf6   }{\fs24 A psionicist receives 35 c
haracter points to spend on class abilities. Abilities cost 5 to 15 points. Any unspent points can be saved to buy proficiencies or saved for use in the game. 
\par }\pard \fi180\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 All psionicists use Table 78: Psionicist Saving Throws and MTHAC0s from Table 77: THAC0s & MTHAC
0. Psionicists use the THAC0s from Table 77 unless they purchase better combat abilities during character creation. All psionicists use Table 79: Psionicist Experience Levels. Psionicists use Table 80: Psionic Progression unless they purchase better psych
ic abilities during character creation. All of these tables appear in Chapter 9 Psionics of this book.
\par Psionicist roll six-sided dice to determine hit points unless they purchase larger hit dice.
\par Unless stated otherwise, a character can take each ability only once and only when the character is first created.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Armor Use (5/10):}{\fs24  The psionicist can employ small shields and padded, leather, studded leather, or hide armor. As a 10-point ability the psionicist can use small or medium shields, any of the armor typ
es listed above, plus brigandine, chain mail, ring mail, scale mail, or metal lamellar armor. If the psionicist does not take this ability, he can wear no armor and cannot employ shields.
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Attack Mode of Choice (10):}{\fs24  The psionicist develops extra skill in using one particular psionic attack mode and gains a +1 bonus to mental attack rolls when using that attack mode. This ability is useless without the contact ability.

\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Combat Bonus (10):}{\fs24  The psionicist uses the priest THAC0 chart.
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Contact (5/10):}{\fs24  The psionicist receives the contact proficiency and gains attack modes as shown on the Psionic Progression table in the }{\i\fs24 Skills & Powers}{\fs24  book. As a 10-point ability
, the psionicist receives extra attack modes as though he was two levels higher than his actual level. For example, a 1st-level psionicist would receives two attack modes. The character can never have more than five attack modes. If the psionicist does no
t take this power, he can purchase the contact proficiency any time he has five character points available.
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Followers (5/10):}{\fs24  The psionicist becomes a contemplative master at 9th level. A 1st level psionicist arrives each month to study with the master. Stu
dents serve without pay if they receive at least 10 hours of training each week (they leave to seek new masters if they do not receive sufficient training). The maximum number of students the master attracts is equal to one half the master's Charisma scor
e
, rounded down. If the master builds a sanctuary, he can attract a number of students equal to his Charisma score. As a 10-point ability, the psionicist becomes a renowned teacher and can attract students at any level, subject to the limits noted above. I
f the psionicist does not choose this ability, he never attracts followers, but can hire servants and henchmen for pay just as any other character can.
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Guarded Mind (5/10):}{\fs24  The psionicist can block or resist attempts to usurp his will and gains a +1 bonus t
o all saving throws against spells from the enchantment/charm school. As a 10-point ability, the psionicist gains a +2 bonus to all saving throws against spells from the enchantment/charm school.
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Hit Point Bonus (10):}{\fs24  Psionicists with this ability roll eight-sided dice for hit points rather than six-sided dice. The psionicist still gains only two extra hit points per level at 10th level and beyond.
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Mental Defense (5/10):}{\fs24  The psionicist can close his mind to psychic contact and gains defense modes as shown on the Psionic progression table in the }{\i\fs24 Skills & Powers}{\fs24 
 book. The psionicist also receives a +2 bonus to his mental armor class. As a 10-point ability, the psionicist receives extra defense modes as though he was two levels higher than his actual level. For
 example, a 1st-level psionicist would receives two defense modes. The character can never have more than five defense modes. If the psionicist does not take this power, he has an open mind, just as if he were a non-psionic character. If the psionicist do
es not choose this ability at the beginning of play, he can purchase the five-point version whenever he has five character points to spend. The 10-point version is available only at the beginning of play.
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Penetrating Mind (10):}{\fs24  The psionicist can penetrate 
physical barriers with his mind more readily than other psionicists can. It takes two inches of lead or iron, four inches of obsidian, or two feet of rock to block the psionicist's clairsentient and telepathic powers. Note that most psionic powers require
 line of sight; this ability does not negate a blocked line of sight (see }{\i\fs24 Skills & Powers,}{\fs24 
 page 150). This ability has no effect on psionic combat and does not allow the psionicist to ignore magical or psychic barriers that block psionic powers.
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 PSP bonus (10): }{\fs24 
The psionicist has a potent mind and rolls eight-sided dice for psionic strength points instead of six-sided dice. The psionicist still gains only three extra PSPs plus his Wisdom bonus per level at 10th level and beyond.
