\par }{\fs28\cf12 Kits}{\fs24   There are a few rules for players to follow when selecting character kits.
\par \tab A player may not choose a kit that is barred to his character\rquote s class or race. In the case of multi\_classed characters, if the kit is barred to any of the character\rquote s classes, he may not select that kit.
\par \tab A player can have only one kit per character, and the selection must be made during character creation. The only exception is if these rules are added to an already existing AD&D game campaign. In this case, the 
DM and players can agree on an appropriate kit for each character.
\par \tab Once a kit is chosen, the player cannot later change it. For example, if a character has the peasant hero kit, and over the course of a long, successful campaign he becomes the ruler of hi
s homeland, he does not now assume the noble kit. He remains a peasant hero. Characters cannot change their pasts.
\par \tab Remember, a character with a kit can purchase any of the recommended weapon and nonweapon proficiencies (but not recommended traits) listed for 1 character point less than the cost detailed in the proficiency section.
\par \tab In general, any of the following kits can be used with any character class. Some combinations, such as paladin/thug are not allowed. Let common sense, the campaign setting, and 
the DM serve as guides. These kits also can apply to the NPCs inhabiting a DM\rquote s campaign. If a player wants to randomly select a kit, he can use Table 41. The table also can be used to generate NPCs.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Acrobat}{\fs24   An acrobat is a general term for performers of amazing physical feats. These include jugglers, tumblers, jesters, and tightrope\_
walkers. Whatever their specialty, these characters make a living by entertaining others. Acrobats often travel in groups or w
ith circuses or carnivals. These shows wander from town to town and castle to castle. All levels of society wish to be entertained. As such, successful acrobats find themselves in much demand.
\par \tab A life on the road is not an easy one, however, and many acrobats often turn to other avenues to make money. Their dexterous skills make them valuable adventurers, especially if some larceny or petty theft is involved.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Social ranks:}{\fs24  Acrobats most often occupy the middle tier of a society. Most lower\_ranked members o
f a society have not the time to develop skills, like those of the acrobat. They must concentrate on putting food on the table. Roll 2d6 to determine an acrobat\rquote s social rank at the campaign\rquote s beginning.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx1440\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 \tab }{\b\fs24 2d6 roll\tab Social rank
\par }{\fs24 \tab 2\endash 8\tab Lower Middle Class
\par \tab 9\endash 12\tab Upper Middle Class
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Requirements:}{\fs24  To take this kit, a character must have a minimum Dexterity/Balance of 14 and a minimum Strength/Stamina of 12. The acrobat kit is barred to half\_
ogres, as well as any optional PC race that is size large (restriction z from the Other Races section of Chapter Three).
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Weapon proficiencies:}{\fs24  Small, light weapons are preferred by acrobats, as bulky or heavy ones would hinder their agile maneuvers. Suggested weapons include the knife, dagger, short sword, club, and hand axe. T
hrown weapons and those with long hafts or handles also are common choices among acrobats, as the weapons can be used to juggle or pole\_vault. These weapons include: quarterstaff, dart, javelin, and spear.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Recommended nonweapon proficiencies:}{\fs24  Disguise, juggling, jumping, musical instrument, tightrope\_walking, and tumbling.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Equipment:}{\fs24  Acrobats prefer to be lightly armed and armored to allow for the fullest range of movement.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Recommended traits:}{\fs24  Ambidexterity, double\_jointed, glibness.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Benefits:}{\fs24  If unarmored, acrobats receive a +2 bonus to tumbling, tightrope\_walking, and jumping proficiency checks. In addition, they gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class versus hurled missile weapons\emdash 
provided they have room to dodge the attack and are not otherwise prevented from moving freely.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Hindrances:}{\fs24  Any acrobat who wears armor heavier than studded leather (AC 7) suffers a \endash 1 penalty to tumbling, tightrope\_
walking, and jumping proficiency checks per point of armor class better than AC 7. For example, an acrobat wearing chain mail\emdash AC5\emdash suffers a \endash 
2 penalty. Note that Dexterity or magical bonuses to Armor Class do not increase this penalty. An acrobat wearing studded leather armor, a }{\i\fs24 ring of protection +2}{\fs24 , and having a 15 Dexterity would incur no penalty despite his AC 4 rating.

\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Wealth:}{\fs24  Acrobats receive the normal amount of starting cash appropriate to their class.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf12 Amazon}{\fs24   In Amazon cultures, the women are the leaders, rulers, generals, and warriors, while the men are the cooks, cleaners, homemakers, and simple laborers\emdash if not
 the outright slaves or property of the women. Such matriarchal societies may be large or small, savage or friendly. Amazon women can be seen as brusque, rude, haughty, or domineering by those from male\_
dominated cultures. The Amazons of legend were fierce combatants and famous riders and breeders of magnificent horses. As such, many Amazons prefer light armor, weapons, and equipment.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Social ranks:}{\fs24  Amazon women can come from any economic background. Roll 2d6 to determine the rank of an Amazon female. Males are considered lower class.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx1440\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 \tab }{\b\fs24 2d6 roll\tab Social rank
\par }{\fs24 \tab 2\tab Lower class
\par \tab 3\endash 5\tab Lower middle class
\par \tab 6\endash 10\tab Upper middle class
\par \tab 11\endash 12\tab Upper class
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Requirements: }{\fs24 Female characters of any demihuman or humanoid race can choose this kit.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Weapon proficiencies:}{\fs24 
 Amazons can choose from: battle axe, bow (any), club, dagger, hand or throwing axe, javelin, knife, lance, spear, staff, sword (any). Men are allowed only one initial weapon proficiency, and it must be from the above list.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Recommended nonweapon proficiencies:}{\fs24  Riding (land\_based), rope use, engineering, navigation, endurance, animal training, animal handling, armorer, bowyer/fletcher, hunting, running, set snares, survival, tracking.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Equipment:}{\fs24  Amazons can begin with only the following types of armor: shi
eld, leather, padded, studded leather, scale mail, hide, banded mail, or bronze plate mail. Better armor can be had once a character has ventured to other cities.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Recommended traits:}{\fs24  Allure, animal empathy, keen senses, obscure knowledge.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Benefits:}{\fs24  Amazo
ns are fierce, eager competitors. Many male opponents underestimate them. As a result, in any melee combat where an Amazon is fighting a male opponent, the Amazon gains a +2 bonus to her first attack and damage roll. Thereafter combat is run normally.

\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Hindrances: }{\fs24 Amazons suffer a \endash 2 reaction roll penalty from NPCs of male\_dominated societies. Over time, this penalty should be reduced or eliminated if the NPCs become accustomed to the strong\_willed ways of the Amazon.

\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Wealth:}{\fs24  Amazons begin the game with the amount of money appropriate to their classes. 
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf12 Animal Master}{\fs24   Animal masters have an affinity with nature\rquote s creatures. They can be trainers, keepers, or guardians of animals. Good\_aligned animal masters protect and care for animals, evil ones use simple
 creatures to their own advantage. Many animal masters spend much of their time outside with their furred, feathered, or scaled friends. Animal masters could include rangers, huntsmen, falconers, and druids.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Social ranks:}{\fs24  Animal masters tend to be earthy folks from the lower echelons of a community. Roll 2d6 to determine an animal master\rquote s rank.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx1440\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 \tab }{\b\fs24 2d6 roll\tab Social rank}{\fs24 
\par \tab 2\endash 5\tab Lower Class
\par \tab 6\endash 11\tab Lower Middle Class
\par \tab 12\tab Upper Middle Class
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Requirements:}{\fs24  To take this kit, a character must have a minimum Constitution/Fitness of 10 and a minimum Wisdom/Intuition of 12. This kit is open to all player character races.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Weapon proficiencies:}{\fs24  Animal masters can use any weapon appropriate to their class.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Recommended nonweapon proficiencies:}{\fs24  Animal lore, survival, agriculture, animal training, animal handling, fire\_building, fishing, herbalism, hunting, mountaineering, riding (any), swimming, set snares, tracking.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Equipment:}{\fs24  Standard for the character\rquote s class.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Recommended traits:}{\fs24  Animal empathy, empathy, climate sense.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Benefits:}{\fs24  When this kit is chosen, the player and DM must determine a suitable animal companion for the character. There are several factors to consider: 1) the climate and terrain of the animal master\rquote 
s homeland, where he acquired the companion; 2) the character\rquote s alignment, as companions are attracted only to animal masters of like demeanor; 3) the character\rquote 
s race (dwarves and gnomes might attract burrowing or underground creatures, while elves would attract forest creatures) and; 4) the availability of compatibl
e creatures. All animal companions should be size S (small). An animal companion is similar to a wizard\rquote 
s familiar in that it has a bond with the animal master. The master can issue it simple verbal commands, and the animal can convey its needs and emotions.
\par \tab After making a list of available and compatible creatures, the player should choose one creature as a companion. DMs might prefer the animal to be selected randomly. If this is the case, roll 1d20 and consult the chart below.
\par 
