\par }{\fs28\cf6 Character Class Restrictions  }{\fs24 Non\_warrior characters are normally restricted by the rules dictating the ty
pes of weapons they can acquire proficiencies for. However, by spending extra character points for a weapon proficiency slot, a character can purchase a proficiency that he would otherwise not be able to possess.
\par \tab A rogue or a priest can acquire a proficiency for a weapon that is normally restricted to a warrior\rquote s use. One additional character point must be spent when the slot is purchased\emdash 
the slot will cost 4 points, instead of the 3 rogues and priests usually pay.
\par \tab 
A wizard can spend 2 additional character points to become proficient in a weapon normally allowed to a priest or a rogue. If the wizard wishes to become proficient with a weapon that is normally limited to fighters, however, he must spend 3 extra charac
ter points. 
