\par }{\fs28\cf6 Recording Bulk (Optional Rule)
\par }{\fs24 \tab In addition to weight, the items of equipment are given a bulk rating\emdash an expansion of the earlier categories S, M, and L. The bulk ratings are separate from weight, and represent how much space each object takes up. 
\par }\pard\plain \s1\keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx2880\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel0\adjustright {\tab Small Size (S) \tab =0, 1, 2 bulk points
\par }\pard\plain \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx2880\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20 {\fs24 \tab Medium Size (M) \tab =3, 4, 5 bulk points
\par \tab Large Size (L)\tab =6* or more bulk points
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 
\par *Some large objects, particularly weapons, will actually have lower bulk points than 6. Since the weapon size is primarily a factor of length, these items can be transported with relative ease.
\par \tab Players who want the added realism can keep track of how many
 points of bulk they are carrying. The rule is especially useful for planning a trading caravan and calculating how many goods an individual porter or beast of burden can carry. Vessels such as packs and pouches are limited in how much bulk they can carry
: 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Backpacks }{\fs24 can vary in size, and they hold an amount of bulk equal to a character\rquote s Strength score.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Belt pouches}{\fs24  can hold up to 3 bulk points. A single character can wear no more than two belt pouches.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Saddlebags}{\fs24  (horse or mule) can hold up to 4 bulk points, and each animal carries two saddlebags. The capacities of some other animals include (per saddlebag): dog=1; donkey/burro=3; camel=10; elephant=20.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Effects of Bulk}{\fs24 
\par \tab 
A human character can carry an amount of bulk equal to his Strength/Stamina score without suffering any ill effects. If he tries to carry more bulk than his score allows, he suffers one penalty in encumbrance class. For example, if Blutar, with a Strength
/Stamina of 17, is loaded down with 20 bulk points of light material, his encumbrance might only be Light, but for game purposes it is treated as Moderate.
\par \tab Smaller characters can carry less than their Strength/Stamina score in bulk before they suffer the encumbrance penalty, as follows:
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Halflings}{\fs24  and }{\b\fs24 gnomes}{\fs24  can carry 1/2 their Str/Stamina score in bulk.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Elves}{\fs24  can carry their Strength/Stamina \endash 3 in bulk points.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Dwarves}{\fs24  can carry their Strength/Stamina \endash 1.
\par \tab A character\rquote s weapon does not count toward his bu
lk rating, though a shield does. Armor is not counted as bulk, but it has the effect of lowering the total bulk the character could otherwise bear. See the equipment tables to determine the capacity penalties for each type of armor.
\par \tab No character can carry more than twice his Strength/Stamina score in bulk.
\par 
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Recording Encumbrance (Simplified)
\par }{\fs24 \tab Characters can simplify the recording of encumbrance for purposes of the Skills and Powers rules. For most encounters, determine the character\rquote s encumbrance by consi
dering only his armor, shield and largest weapon. These are generally the most significant parts of his load, and thus will provide a reasonably accurate rating.
\par \tab If the character is carrying camping or exploring equipment, or trade goods, extra supplies, 
etc., the additional encumbrance also can be simplified. If the character is carrying a backpack, figure 10 pounds if he has miscellaneous exploring equipment (rope, lantern, oil, spikes, etc.), 20 pounds for camping equipment (bedroll, cloak or spare clo
thes, tinderbox and food). Add only five\_pound increments for extra items\emdash trade goods, treasure, extra oil flasks, etc.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Weight
\par }{\fs24 \tab The equipment tables at the end of this chapter contain a weight for every listed item. Players and DMs can use these weights to calculate exact character loads.
