\par }{\fs36\cf6 Chapter 9:
\par Psionics
\par }{\fs24 
\par }{\fs28\cf12 Psionics  }{\fs24 With psionics, a character can read the minds of others, move objects without physically touching them, or travel across vast distances in an ins
tant. This chapter explains the game mechanics used to run psionic characters and provides enough powers to get wild talent and psionicist heroes started. Consider the definitions of the following terms:
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Psionics:}{\fs24  The practice of extraordinary psychic pow
ers. A character who has psionic abilities harnesses the power of his or her mind to produce a particular effect. Characters who have psionic powers are either psionicists or wild talents.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Psionicist:}{\fs24  A character who uses the force of his or her mind to affect the environment and inhabitants around them.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Wild Talent:}{\fs24  A character from any class who has a natural psionic ability and at least one psionic power.
\par \tab The psionic system presented in this chapter provides descriptions of the core powers. This chapter presents the same psionics rules that appear in the revised Dark Sun boxed set. 
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 What\rquote s Different?
\par }{\fs24 \tab If players are new to psionics, skip this section because the changes to the original rules from }{\i\fs24 The Complete Psionics Handbook}{\fs24  discussed below may be c
onfusing. If players are familiar with the previous psionics rules, then a brief discussion of the changes to look for should be noted.
\par \tab Many of the terms and powers used in }{\i\fs24 The Complete Psionics Handbook}{\fs24  have been retained for this new system. However, th
e definitions and descriptions may have changed, so read this section carefully. The most important changes to watch for are the following:
\par 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\b\i\fs24 Attack and defense}{\fs24  modes are no longer powers, but bonus proficiencies. The new terms are psionic attacks and ps
ionic defenses. Psionicists gain psionic attacks and defenses automatically by level advancement. Existing characters with attack modes must select other telepathic devotions to replace them.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\fs24 The }{\b\i\fs24 contact power}{\fs24 
 is now the contact bonus proficiency. The proficiency allows characters to participate in psionic combat. In addition, psionic combat has been simplified to work like other AD&D combat forms (that is, using attack and damage rolls). Characters who had th
e contact power must select another telepathic devotion to replace it.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\b\i\fs24 Tangents }{\fs24 have been eliminated.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\b\i\fs24 Maintenance costs}{\fs24  for powers have been eliminated. All powers now have a standard PSP cost per round of use and can be maintained each round by paying that cost.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\b\i\fs24 Power scores}{\fs24  and the optional effects of rolls of power scores and 20s have been eliminated. All characters now have }{\i\fs24 mental armor classes}{\fs24  (MAC) and }{\i\fs24 mental attack numbers}{\fs24 
 (MTHAC0). MTHAC0 stands for \ldblquote mental THAC0\rdblquote  or \ldblquote mental attack roll.\rdblquote  Th
e acronym refers to the number (or higher) a particular character needs to roll on 1d20 to hit an opponent with a mental armor class of 0. This mechanic has two distinct uses that work in basically the same manner.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\fs24 The }{\b\i\fs24 power check}{\fs24  has been eliminated. To determine the successful use of a psionic power, a character makes an }{\i\fs24 MTHAC0 roll}{\fs24 
. In psionic combat, a character makes MTHAC0 rolls to break through a target\rquote s mental defenses and open the mind. To use a psionic power on an open mind, an MTHAC0 roll is made against the power\rquote s MAC instead of the target\rquote 
s MAC. (All psionic powers have base MAC scores.) Some minds are considered open automatically (like the psionicist\rquote s own mind for the purposes of using a power on himself). In these cases, no psionic combat is needed, for the mind is already open.

\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\fs24 The }{\b\i\fs24 metapsionics discipline}{\fs24  has been eliminated; its powers have been redistributed among the remaining five disciplines.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 
\par }{\fs28\cf12 Using Psionics}{\fs24   Psionic energy can be shaped and used by psioni
cists and wild talents to produce desired effects, called psionic powers.  All psionic powers are grouped into one of five categories, or disciplines, based on how the energy is used. The major powers of a given discipline are called sciences.
\par \tab Two key concepts need to be presented before the rules for using psionics in the AD&D game are detailed. These are }{\b\i\fs24 psionic strength points (PSPs)}{\fs24  and }{\b\i\fs24 mental attack rolls (MTHAC0s).}{\fs24  These are described below.

\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Psionic Strength Points (PSPs):}{\fs24  Every psionic character ha
s an internal store of psionic energy, represented as psionic strength points. These are used to activate sciences and devotions, to focus psionic attacks, and to determine how much psionic damage a hero\rquote s psionic defenses can stand.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Mental Attack Rolls:}{\fs24  
The success of psionic attacks against closed minds is determined by the number a character needs to roll on 1d20 to hit a specific mental armor class (MAC). The mental attack number (MTHAC0) is the number the character needs to hit a MAC of 0. When used 
on open minds, the roll is made against a power\rquote s MAC. Each power has a base MAC number used to determine the difficulty of activating a psionic power against an open mind.
\par \tab All }{\b\i\fs24 psionic powers}{\fs24  belong to one of five }{\b\i\fs24 disciplines}{\fs24 : clairsentience, psychokinesis
, psychometabolism, psychoportation, and telepathy. Within each discipline, the powers are divided into two categories: major powers, or }{\i\fs24 sciences}{\fs24 ; and minor powers, or }{\i\fs24 devotions}{\fs24 
. The five disciplines are defined as follows:
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Clairsentient}{\fs24  powers allow characters to perceive things beyond the natural range of human and demihuman senses.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Psychokinetic powers}{\fs24  move objects across space using only the energy of the mind.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Psychometabolic powers}{\fs24  affect the user\rquote s body by altering it in some manner.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Psychoportive powers}{\fs24  allow psionic travel, moving characters from one location to another without crossing space.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Telepathic powers}{\fs24  involve the direct contact of two or more minds.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Closed and Open Minds
\par }{\fs24 \tab The minds of all characters and creatures exist in one of two states: either }{\i\fs24 closed}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 open}{\fs24 
. A closed mind has either natural or enhanced defenses that protect it from unwanted intrusion. Only those things that enter through the normal senses (such as sight, sound, taste, touch, or smell) can impact on a closed mind. }{\b\i\fs24 
The minds of all characters and creatures are naturally closed.}{\fs24  A character can voluntarily open his or her mind to psionic contact, or a closed mind can be opened by psionic attack.
\par \tab An open mind is not a natural state. For a mind to be open, psionic defenses must be voluntarily lowered (in the case of a willing subject) or breached by psionic attack (in an unwilling opponent). A psionicist\rquote 
s own mind is considered open when using a psionic power with an area of effect of \ldblquote personal\rdblquote  (such as the heightened senses devotion).
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Mental Armor Class (MAC)
\par }{\fs24 \tab All characters and creatures have mental armor classes (MACs). While physical Armor Classes protect a body from physical attacks, MACs provide protection from psionic attacks. The MAC rating ranges from minima
l defense (MAC 10) to maximum defense (MAC \endash 10); there are no MACs worse than 10 or better than \endash 10.
\par \tab As with standard Armor Class, the higher the MAC number, the more vulnerable the character is to psionic attack. Likewise, with all attacks, a roll of 20 always hits and a roll of 1 always misses, regardless of the target\rquote s MAC number.
\par 
\par 
\par For those who have copies of }{\i\fs24 The Complete Psionics Handbook}{\fs24  and who want to continue using the \ldblquote optional results\rdblquote  rules (page 28), make the following change. A roll of a power\rquote 
s MAC score gives the good result (what used to be signified by a roll of the power score), while a roll of 1 gives the bad result (what used to happen on a roll of 20).
\par 
\par 
\par \tab To determine a base MAC number, find the character\rquote s Wisdom score on Table 74 below. Then find the character\rquote s Intelligence score and add the indicated MAC modifier. MACs can be imp
roved through proficiencies and other means, as detailed later.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Table 74: Base MAC and PSP Bonuses
