\par }{\fs28\cf6 Closing an Open Mind
\par }{\fs24 \tab A nonpsionic mind is one that has never had any PSPs. Its natural state is closed unless willingly opened or opened by psionic means. If such a target\rquote s mind has 
been opened, but the subsequent psionic attack or power used against it wasn\rquote t successful, the target can attempt to re\_
close its mind in the next round. This requires a saving throw vs. paralyzation at no penalty. If a psionic power was used successfully against the newly opened nonpsionic mind, the target can still attempt to close its mind, but its saving throw is at a 
\endash 4 penalty. The target may attempt to close its mind every round thereafter.
\par \tab For a newly opened psionic mind (one whose PSPs have been reduced to 0), the target can\rquote t attempt to re\_close its mind until 1d4+1 rounds have passed. After the required rounds have passed, the target can make a Wisdom check at a \endash 
3 penalty every round thereafter to attempt to close its mind.
\par \tab When either a nonpsionic or psionic character succeeds at re\_closing his mind, the following occurs: any psionic power currently in use against the character ceases to function, and contact between the two minds is broken. If the power\rquote 
s effect already took place in the round in which the mind re\_closed, the psionicist expends the full PSP cost. If the power\rquote s effect didn\rquote t take place yet in the round, then the lower PSP cost is subtracted from the psionicist\rquote 
s PSP total (as if the activation attempt failed). If the psionicist wants to reestablish contact, he\rquote ll have to once again open the target\rquote s mind.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Psionics in a Round
\par }{\fs24 \tab A psionicist can do several actions during a single round. He can:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\fs24 Make as many psionic attacks as his experience level indicates.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\fs24 Use one psionic defense.
