\ls1\adjustright {\fs24 Maintain as many previously successfully activated powers as he wishes, provided he can afford to continue paying the PSP 
costs. Further, if a psionic attack succeeds and opens a closed mind, a psionic power can be used against the mind that same round.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Limitations to Psionic Powers
\par }{\fs24 \tab Psionic powers have definite limitations. Some of these already have been discussed, but are repeated here to emphasize them. Other limitations are new.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\b\fs24 PSPs:}{\fs24  Psionicists and wild talents have a finite amount of psionic strength available to them at any given time. This strength, expressed as PSPs, must be expended to use psionic attacks, defe
nses, and powers. The total also indicates how much damage a hero\rquote 
s psionic defenses can withstand before his mind opens. As such, the psionic character must always balance the use of powers, attacks, and defenses with how strong he wants his own internal walls to remain.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\b\fs24 Line of Sight:}{\fs24  All psionic attacks and most powers require line of sight to use. If line of sight is blocked, most psionics won\rquote t work.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\b\fs24 Touch: }{\fs24 Some psionic powers have a range of \ldblquote touch.\rdblquote  These can be used in melee combat, but they require a physical attack roll }{\i\fs24 and}{\fs24 
 an MTHAC0 roll to work. Like all psionic powers, they only can be used against open minds.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}
\ls1\adjustright {\b\fs24 Obstructions: }{\fs24 Anything that hinders a character\rquote s normal vision blocks line of sight. Unless the description states otherwise, p
sionicists require a line of sight to use a power. Obvious exceptions to this rule are the clairsentient powers and many of the telepathic powers. However, certain materials can obstruct these psionic powers if they completely block the target. These are 
lead and iron (at least 1 inch thick), obsidian (at least 2 inches thick), stone (at least 1 foot thick), and the }{\i\fs24 antimagic shell}{\fs24  spell.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright {\fs24 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Psychic Contests
\par }{\fs24 \tab Sometimes two or more psionicists try to use a psionic power on the same target. For example, two psi
onicists might try to use telekinesis to move a stone in two different directions, or they might attempt to teleport the same character to different locations, or they might use any psionic powers in such a way as to be in direct conflict with each other.
 Which power use prevails? The struggle results in a psychic contest.
\par \tab To resolve a psychic contest, compare the competing characters\rquote  MTHAC0 rolls made to activate the powers. The character who has the lowest successful MTHAC0 roll wins the contest. If non
e of the competing characters roll successfully, none of the power uses succeed. If one character succeeds and the others fail the rolls, then that character wins the contest. If competing characters have the same MTHAC0 score and they roll the same numbe
rs on the dice, then a psychic lock occurs.
\par \tab In a psychic lock, neither competing character wins the psychic contest that round. Both are applying equal psionic pressure, thus creating a stalemate. To resolve the contest, both characters must pay the power\rquote 
s PSP cost and engage in another round of psychic contest. If either character fails to pay the cost\emdash effectively giving up\emdash that character suffers a psychic backlash and loses 4d4 PSPs immediately.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Psionics and Magic
\par }{\fs24 \tab Psionics and magic use completely different forces. Psionics uses internal energy, while magic taps into extraplanar power. Both arts can produce similar effects, but they do so in very different ways. For this reason, psionics and magic don
\rquote t ordinarily mix. Magical spells, for instance, can\rquote t be used to detect or dispel psionic activity, unless otherwise stated. Likewise, psionic powers can\rquote 
t detect magic that simulates psionic abilities. Lastly, if a psionicist uses a psychokinetic, psychometabolic, psychoportive, or telepathic power against
 a magical illusion, he automatically gets a saving throw vs. spell to disbelieve it. Specific spells, as listed below, intermix with psionics in the following ways.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Antimagic shell:}{\fs24  This spell blocks the effects of psionic powers.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Detect charm:}{\fs24  This spell detects telepathic control, such as domination.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Detect invisibility:}{\fs24  This spell allows the caster to see clearly psionic invisibility, astral travelers, shadowform, and ethereal creatures. It doesn\rquote t work against characters in other dimensions.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Detect magic:}{\fs24  This spell has no effect on psionics.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Detect scrying:}{\fs24  This spell will detect psionic scrying, though psionicists get a save vs. spell to avoid detection.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 ESP:}{\fs24  If this spell is used against psionicists, they get a save vs. spell with a +2 bonus to negate the effects.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 False vision:}{\fs24  This spell works against psionics, though psionicists get a save vs. spell to negate effects.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Forbiddance:}{\fs24  This spell effectively blocks all teleportation and metabolic powers.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Free action:}{\fs24  This spell overcomes all psychokinetic effects against the subject\rquote s body, as well as domination.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Globe of invulnerability/minor globe of invulnerability:}{\fs24  These spells have no effect on psionics.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Magic jar:}{\fs24  Psionicists use their combined Wisdom and Constitution scores when determining the differential modifier.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Mind blank:}{\fs24  Psionicists get a save vs. spell to overcome this enchantment.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Misdirection:}{\fs24  This spell has no effect on psionics.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Mislead:}{\fs24  A psionic attack reveals this spell, but the first attack automatically fails.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Nondetection:}{\fs24  This spell works normally against psionics.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Otiluke\rquote s resilient sphere:}{\fs24  Psionics can\rquote t penetrate this spell\rquote s protection.
\par \tab Protection from evil/protection from evil, 10\_foot radius: These spells provide +2 bonuses to MACs.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Spell immunity:}{\fs24  This spell has no effect on psionics.
\par \tab }{\b\i\fs24\cf6 Trap the soul:}{\fs24  Psionicists trapped by this spell can\rquote t use any psionic powers.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Psionicists and 
\par Wild Talents
\par }{\fs24 
\par \tab Psionic powers can be used by any character class, though one class specializes in the use of psionics:
 the psionicist. Wild talents are a subclassification within other character classes. These characters possess one or two psionic powers. Their main vocation is that of their class. For instance, a priest could have a psionic ability or two, but he relies
 primarily on the skills of his class. A psionicist, on the other hand, relies almost entirely on his psionic gifts. The differences between the two types of psionic characters are explained in the section that follows.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf12 Psionicist }{\fs24  The psionicist character works to mold mind, body, and spirit into a unified, powerful whole. The hero\rquote s internal energy, or psionic strength, comes from deep within himself\emdash 
from a place psionicists call the nexus. This energy is given form and purpose by the individual\rquote s strengt
h of will. Through extraordinary discipline, long contemplation, and deepening awareness of self, the psionicist taps the vast potential of his mind.
\par \tab Psionicists must meet or exceed the following prerequisites.
\par }{\b\fs24 Ability requirements:}{\fs24  Constitution 11, Intelligence 12, Wisdom 15
\par }{\b\fs24 Prime requisites:}{\fs24  Wisdom, Constitution
\par }{\b\fs24 Races allowed: }{\fs24 Any
\par \tab Because the pursuit of psionics require strict mental and physical discipline, a psionicist has two prime requisites: Wisdom and Constitution. His prima
ry mental ability score is Wisdom. As the measure of his willpower and enlightenment, Wisdom promotes the understanding and mastery of the inner self\emdash 
the essence of psionic ability. Likewise, the tremendous stress of using psionics requires a healthy body 
to house a fit mind. This is where Constitution comes into play. Lastly, Intelligence is important to psionicists because of the reasoning and memorization necessary to the class.
\par \tab All races eligible for use as player characters can become psionicists. Human psionicists have no limit on the levels of experience they can attain in their chosen class. Half\_elves, half\_orcs, and half\_
ogres (due to their partial human heritage) can reach 12th level. Halflings and gnomes can attain 10th level. Dwarves and elves can reach only 8th level as psionicists. All creatures not listed here can reach 10th level.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Dual\_Classed and 
\par Multiclassed Psionicists
\par }{\fs24 A human character who has scores of 15 or more in the prime requisites of his first class and scores of 17 or more in the prime requisites of the class he switches to can be a dual\_classed psionicist. See the }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote s Handbook}{
\fs24 , for more details on dual\_class benefits and restrictions.
\par \tab Demihuman characters can be multiclassed psionicists if they meet the requirements in the }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote s Handbook}{\fs24 .
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Alignment
\par }{\fs24 \tab Psionicists can be of any alignment, save chaotic. The discipline integral to psionics can\rquote t be maintained by chaotic characters. If a psionicist\rquote s alignment shifts to chaotic for any reason, he quickly begins to lose psion
ic powers. Every day his alignment remains chaotic, the character must make an ability check against one\_
half his Wisdom score, rounded down. Each time the character fails this check, he loses access to one psionic discipline and all the powers related to it. The discipline is selected randomly by the DM.
\par \tab Psionicists who change to chaotic alignment can\rquote t recover PSPs. If a psionicist\rquote s alignment turns from chaotic back to nonchaotic, he begins to recover lost disciplines at a rate of one per day. This is a
ccomplished by making the same halved Wisdom check described above\emdash success indicates the return of a random discipline from those that were lost.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Weapon and Armor Restrictions
\par }{\fs24 \tab Psionicists disdain using weapons of any sort. Further, they don\rquote t have the time to properly train in their use. If a psionicist character wants to use a weapon, he must select it from the following small\_
sized items: hand crossbow, dagger, dart, dirk, knife, scourge, sickle, and short sword.
\par \tab Psionicists can only use the following types of armor: padded, leather, studded leather, and hide. They may also carry small shields.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Psionicist Benefits
\par }{\fs24 \tab Psionicists have their own THAC0s, which are listed on the THAC0s and MTHAC0s, above, along with their respective MTHAC0s. MTHAC0s for wild talents are listed on the same table, though these characters must refer to their class\rquote 
s own THAC0 tables for calculated attack rolls.
\par \tab Psionicists gain a +2 bonus on all saving throws vs. enchantment/charm spells. This is in addition to any magical defense adjustments for high Wisdom scores. the Psionicist Saving Throw table lists saving throws for this character class.
\par \tab At 9th level, a psionicist becomes a contemplative master. Such a master can build a sanctuary to use as his headquarters and can attract followers. A 1st\_
level psionicist arrives monthly to study with the master, regardless of whether he builds a sanctuary. The maximum number of followers is equal to the master\rquote s Charisma score if he builds a sanctuary, or half that number rounded down if he doesn
\rquote t.
\par \tab A master\rquote s followers want to learn. They serve in any capacity the master chooses as long as the master spends at least 10 hours per week instructing them. If the master doesn\rquote 
t live up to this schedule, the followers leave to find someone else.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Psionicist Advancement
\par }{\fs24 \tab A psionicist earns experience points and advances in level like members of other classes, as outlined on Table 79 below.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Psionicists and PSPs
\par }{\fs24 \tab A psionicist determines his initial PSP total by adding bonuses awarded for high Wisdom, Constitution, and Intelligence scores to a base of 15, then adding the result of a 1d6 die roll:
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Wis bonus + Con bonus + Int bonus + 15 + 1d6 = 1st\_level PSP total.
\par }{\fs24 \tab With every level increase, up to the 9th level, a psionicist gains additional PSPs by adding the bonuses to a 1d6 die roll:
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Wis bonus + Con bonus + Int bonus + 1d6 = PSPs gained per level (2 through 8).
\par }{\fs24 \tab Starting at 9th level, a psionicist gains just 3 PSPs per level, plus his Wisdom bonus.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24 Wis bonus + 3 = PSPs gained per level (9th level and higher).
\par }{\fs24 
