\par }{\fs28\cf6 Gaining Disciplines and Powers
\par }{\fs24 \tab Every psionic power belongs to one of the five psionic disciplines: }{\i\fs24 clairsentience, psychokinesis, psychometabolism, psychoportation,}{\fs24  and }{\i\fs24 telepathy}{\fs24 . Powers are either major (and are called }{\i\fs24 
sciences}{\fs24 ) or minor (called }{\i\fs24 devotions}{\fs24 ). Before a psionicist can learn a psionic power, he must have access to the appropriate discipline.
\par \tab At 1st level, a psionicist selects one discipline. This is his }{\i\fs24 primary discipline}{\fs24 . As a psionicist advances in level, he gains access to additional disci
plines (as shown on the Psionic Progression table. A psionicist starts out at 1st level with four powers within his primary discipline: one science and three devotions. With each advance in level, the psionicist gains additional disciplines and powers, as
 outlined. Some additional points to consider include the following:
