\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Contact}{\fs24 : This proficiency gives characters access to the psionic attack forms necessary to open a closed mind. Contact allows characters to gain psionic attacks as they become available with level advancement.
\par \tab Psionicists automatically receive this proficiency. It doesn\rquote t take up any of their available slots. As a psionicist increases in level, he automatically receives psionic attack for
ms as outlined on the Psionic Progression table. Psionic attack forms don\rquote t fill up a psionicist\rquote s proficiency slots.
\par \tab Wild talents, on the other hand, must select contact and place it in an available nonweapon proficiency slot if they want to gain its ben
efits. Once contact is slotted, a wild talent selects one psionic attack. He may select an additional attack by placing it in an available nonweapon slot after he has advanced the appropriate number of levels, according to his group\rquote 
s progression rate. Wild talents may never have more than three of the five psionic attack forms.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Harness Subconscious:}{\fs24  Through the use of this proficiency, a psionicist temporarily boosts his PSP total. To procure these extra PSPs, the psionicist\rquote s PSP total must be at its max
imum. Two full days (48 consecutive hours) must be spent gathering energy from subconscious reserves. At the end of this time, the psionicist makes a proficiency check. Success increases his PSP total by 20%, rounded up.
\par \tab The extra PSPs remain available for 72 hours or until they are used up, whichever comes first. At the end of 72 hours, the psionicist loses as many PSPs as he gained from his current total (though the total won\rquote t drop below 0).
\par \tab During the 72 hours of boosted energy, the psionicist can\rquote t recover PSPs if his current total equals or exceeds his usual maximum. Once all of the bonus PSPs have been used, PSPs can be recovered normally up to the usual maximum.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Meditative Focus:}{\fs24  This proficiency allows a psionicist to focus his mental energy into
 one discipline, causing all powers within that discipline to receive MTHAC0 roll bonuses; powers related to other disciplines receive MTHAC0 roll penalties.
\par \tab The psionicist must meditate for 12 consecuti
ve hours. He recovers PSPs normally during this meditative state. When the period ends, the character makes a proficiency check. Success means he has focused his energy into the chosen discipline. All MTHAC0 rolls for powers within that discipline receive
 a +2 bonus for the next 24 hours or until his PSP total is reduced to 0, whichever comes first. All other disciplines get a \endash 1 penalty for the same period.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Mental Armor:}{\fs24  This proficiency allows a character to improve his mental armor class (MAC). Each time this proficiency is placed in an available nonweapon slot, the character\rquote 
s MAC improves. Nonpsionicists improve by +1 for each slot; psionicists improve by +2. The proficiency may only be slotted once per level advancement.
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Rejuvenation:}{\fs24  This proficienc
y allows a psionicist to recover PSPs more quickly than is usual by entering a rejuvenating trance. This state of deep concentration requires a successful proficiency check. For every hour a hero maintains this trance (and makes the check), he regains PSP
s at twice the usual rate (one\_quarter of his total instead of one\_eighth). He can\rquote t expend PSPs while in this trance, and his state is much like deep sleep.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf12 Wild Talents}{\fs24   A wild talent is a hero from any character class other than the psionicist class who
 has natural psionic potential. This potential can be present in any character, regardless of class, alignment, or race. The alignment restrictions of the psionicist class don\rquote t apply to wild talents.
\par \tab Wild talents have one or two psionic powers, up to three psionic defenses, and up to three psionic attacks at their disposal once they\rquote 
ve reached full power. The psionic defenses come naturally, one at a time, according to the Psionic Progression table.
\par \tab Psionic attacks are only gained after the PC places the
 contact proficiency in an available nonweapon proficiency slot. A wild talent chooses one of the five attack forms at that time. He may select a second and a third attack form when slots become available according to his group proficiency progression (as
 outlined in the }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote s Handbook}{\fs24 ).
\par 
